WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.220
Lift a 1000 kg probe from Earth's surface
to a height equal to Earth's radius.

2
00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.720
Use the familiar shortcut
for energy gained,

3
00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.370
and you get about twice the true answer.

4
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.890
The shortcut assumes gravity
stays the same strength.

5
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.550
Up here, it has fallen to a quarter.

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.900
Enter gravitational potential.

7
00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.000
Around a planet, it is
negative everywhere.

8
00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:25.160
Walk outwards from the surface.

9
00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.480
What happens to that negative number?

10
00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:30.490
In this mission, you'll define
gravitational potential,

11
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.990
as work done per unit mass.

12
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:38.120
Then you'll plot potential and field
strength against distance on the same axes.

13
00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: find how the potential
changes as you move away from the planet.
